{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implemented per the operator-ruled design and pushed: Gerrit change 2014 (commit 7ea68f0a12) — https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2014\n\nDesign as landed: new rebar._snapshot.gc_trigger mirrors compact_trigger applied to janitor.run_gc. resolve_gate_handle's attested tail calls maybe_gc — one stat of <store>/gc/last-pass.stamp against the janitor interval_seconds (0 disables), no ticket-store lock in any branch, never raises. When due, a detached child (cwd = the per-host store root) runs the existing run_gc policy under a stamped <store>/gc/worker.lock sidecar (shared stamped_file_is_stale adjudication) plus run_gc's own gc flock; a stand-aside (skipped=\"locked\") does not reset the stamp. Sidecars live in the snapshot store itself — per-host and already canonical, so all worktrees share one clock/lock. Review-bot resident janitor untouched; overlap harmless by construction.\n\nRED→GREEN: tests/unit/test_snapshot_gc_trigger.py (15 tests) — trigger fires on due/missing stamp, gate-resolution wiring (attested fires, local does not), O(1) quiet path (no store enumeration, ticket-store lock patched to fail loudly), single-flight (live lock respected, stale lock reclaimed, run_gc overlap stands aside AND keeps the clock), headline AC end-to-end reclamation on a simulated non-review-bot host, detach argv/cwd/stdio contract, dead-repo-root survival. All RED at collection before the module existed, GREEN after.\n\nVerification: make lint clean, mypy 620 files clean, complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0, targeted suites (snapshot janitor/cache/docs + gate seam tests) pass. One test batch showed a non-reproducing setup ERROR in test_gate_context_seam — traced to my own concurrent 'make typecheck' in the same worktree (mypy running over src while pytest scanned it); 2/2 serial re-runs clean, not a repo bug.\n\nDocs: repo-snapshot-gates.md now documents both GC drivers + the operator force path; ADR 0005 D5 amended (one marker stat in-line; the pass itself stays off every hot path).\n\nNext: wait for LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1 on 2014, Submit, then close."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787337087056651001,"uuid":"b24d4afc-4f0a-44c6-bf4b-681d4a7c5eb4"}